#
# Personal use. Copy to personal.env, mode 0600, and fill in the two values. You make both
# yourself; Robinauts makes neither, reads neither back, and prints neither (CREDENTIALS.md).

# The worker's secret: a long random string you choose, the same the server reads from the
# variable its [workers.claude-container] table names. For example: openssl rand -base64 32
ROBINAUTS_WORKER_SECRET=

# Your Claude subscription token. In your own terminal, with your own Claude Code, run
#     claude setup-token
# approve in the browser, and paste what it prints here. It lasts a year and is yours alone:
# it authenticates with your subscription and may serve nobody else.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Nothing else goes here. In particular no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: it would outrank the token, and
# the worker refuses to start with both.
